     "text": "{\n  \"steps\": [\n    \"Examine UT-AIR telemetry (header_pressure_bar, compressor_current_a, oil_temp_c) leading up to 2026-09-19T21:32:59Z. High compressor current and depleted header pressure would support a major air leak or compressor capacity failure; normal cycling current would refute continuous loaded running.\",\n    \"Examine ST20-WLD telemetry for air_pressure_bar around the stop event. Air pressure dropping below normal range (5.3-5.9 bar) supports localized pneumatic loss or clamp actuator leak at ST20; normal pressure refutes local pneumatic starvation.\",\n    \"Examine ST30-WLD air_pressure_bar to compare against ST20-WLD. Concurrent pressure drop across both stations supports a system-wide compressed air header loss; normal pressure at ST30 while ST20 drops supports an isolated leak or line constriction at ST20.\",\n    \"Examine ST20-WLD process parameters (cycle_time_s, servo_temp_c, weld_current_ka, tip_resistance_mohm). Elevated cycle time or servo temperatures would support a mechanical/servo bind in the weld cell prompting the line lead hold; nominal operation refutes a primary weld process fault.\",\n    \"Assess sensor and data integrity for ST20-WLD air_pressure_bar by inspecting for stuck values, erratic step-discontinuities, or disconnected telemetry. Erratic or static values despite fluctuating header pressure would support a faulty pressure sensor or signal conversion error rather than an actual pneumatic failure.\",\n    \"Review maintenance and operator event logs for UT-AIR and ST20-WLD leading up to the stop timestamp to verify recent pneumatic maintenance, manual shutoff valve adjustments, or filter replacements.\"\n  ],\n  \"upstream_step\": 0,\n  \"sensor_step\": 4,\n  \"suspects\": [\n    \"UT-AIR\",\n    \"ST20-WLD\",\n    \"ST30-WLD\"\n  ]\n} "
